    <string name="rules_gear_title">The equipment</string>
    <string name="rules_gear">12 wooden pins numbered 1 to 12, and a throwing pin: the mölkky. You throw from a line (or a frame, the mölkkaari) laid on the ground.</string>
    <string name="rules_setup_title">Setting up</string>
    <string name="rules_setup">Stand the pins upright, tightly packed, in 4 rows, about 3.5 m from the throwing line (about 4 long adult steps). For children, move the line closer.</string>
    <string name="rules_setup_caption">Starting formation, seen from the throwing line: 1 and 2 at the front, then 3-10-4, then 5-11-12-6, and 7-9-8 at the back.</string>
    <string name="rules_throw_title">Throwing</string>
    <string name="rules_throw">Taking turns, throw the mölkky underarm, feet behind the line. The first throw is often a “strike”: the pins scatter.</string>
    <string name="rules_points_title">Scoring</string>
    <string name="rules_points">One pin down: it scores its number (pin 12 alone = 12 points). Several pins down: count the pins (3 pins = 3 points, all 12 pins = 12 points). A pin leaning on another pin or on the mölkky has not fallen.</string>
    <string name="rules_raise_title">Standing the pins up</string>
    <string name="rules_raise">After each throw, stand the fallen pins back up exactly where they stopped. The game spreads out as it goes on.</string>
    <string name="rules_win_title">Reach exactly 50</string>
    <string name="rules_win">The first to reach exactly 50 points wins. If a throw takes you over 50, your score drops back to 25 and the game goes on.</string>
    <string name="rules_misses_title">Misses</string>
    <string name="rules_misses">A throw that knocks down no pins is a miss. Three misses in a row and the player (or team) is out of the set. A throw that knocks down a pin resets the count.</string>
    <string name="rules_teams_title">Teams and several sets</string>
    <string name="rules_teams">In teams, the teams take turns and, within each team, the players take turns. A round ends when every player or team still in play has thrown. You can play several sets in a row: the app keeps count.</string>
    <string name="rules_variants_title">Variants</string>
    <string name="rules_variants">For a no-pressure game (children, beginners), choose Casual mode when creating the game: no elimination, foot faults ignored, lower target, starting score per player… Casual games count for wins, not for records.</string>
    <string name="rules_faq_title">Frequently asked questions</string>
    <string name="rules_faq_leaning_q">A pin leans against another pin or the mölkky?</string>
    <string name="rules_faq_leaning_a">It does not count as fallen: it must lie fully on the ground. Against a border, a bench or another object on the pitch, it counts as fallen.</string>
    <string name="rules_faq_out_q">A pin goes off the pitch?</string>
    <string name="rules_faq_out_a">On a pitch with a border, put it back one mölkky length from the border. Otherwise, stand it up where it stopped.</string>
    <string name="rules_faq_foot_q">A foot is over the line when throwing?</string>
    <string name="rules_faq_foot_a">That is a foot fault: the throw does not count and counts as a miss (unless Casual mode ignores foot faults).</string>
    <string name="rules_faq_moved_q">A pin is moved by something other than the mölkky (wind, a dog…)?</string>
    <string name="rules_faq_moved_a">Put it back in place: it does not count.</string>

